# state: any
# lane.gpuclock (#433), 2026-10-05: the route text of 1790929514-lane.ibcache-2992454 (route_name
# ibcache-forza-drive, Nova, 420 s held, mark gameplay at the race), unchanged below this header.
# Why not forza-gpuclock (drive.py): on the Thor every Forza run since 10-05 died in its first
# 7-42 s (6 of 6, two refs, no fault line), and on the Nova drive.py stuck on the menus (memfast
# 3557511 / 3557775, 10-03). This blind route reached the race on the Nova in every 10-02 run.
# lane.ibcache (#507) leg 5d: forza414.route's menu phase exactly (boot,
# 14 rounds of START/A; in all three 5b runs on 2026-10-01 that left the race
# running, clock 0:36-0:43 at the first play frame), then a driving pattern
# instead of forza414's, which never moved the car (0 MPH, place 8/8, in
# every play frame of -3202216, -3202498 and -3202829).
#
# The pattern is pgr2.route's: the triggers rest at min; LT full (brake,
# then reverse at a stop) for 2.5 s backs the car off whatever it hit, then
# RT full (throttle) with the stick left, right and centred. A blind
# pattern: it is not known to keep the car on the track, only to keep it
# moving. A `press A` per round answers a results or continue screen (A did
# not move the car in 5b). `mark gameplay` is at the race (see above), so
# the scored window and the static-window check have frames.
wait 20
shot boot20
wait 20
shot boot40
wait 20
mark booted
repeat 14 {
    press START
    wait 5
    shot menu-start
    press A
    wait 5
    shot menu-a
}
mark play
mark gameplay
repeat forever {
    repeat 2 {
        axis RT min
        axis LT max
        wait 2.5
        axis LT min
        axis RT max
        axis LX min
        wait 2.5
        axis LX max
        wait 2.5
        axis LX mid
        wait 2
    }
    axis RT min
    press A
    shot play
}